<title>NETHERLANDS: POLL - Dutch company results week of Aug 4.</title>
<headline>POLL - Dutch company results week of Aug 4.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts' estimates of Dutch company results for the week of August 4:</p>
<p>DATE--COMPANY-----PERIOD--PROFIT------CONSENSUS---RANGE-----PVS</p>
<p> 5/8  KLM	     Q1    net ord ops    115	94/136    271</p>
<p> 5/8  Wolters Kl    H1    net ord ops    245     235/253    206</p>
<p> 6/8  Hoogovens     H1    net pft	  186     162/205    142</p>
<p> 7/8  Reed-Els	H1    comb pre-tax   439     423/460    416</p>
<p> 7/8  RD/Shell	Q2    net pft	 1245    1119/1328  1183</p>
<p> 7/8  RD/Shell	H1    net pft	 2713    2535/2885  2926</p>
<p> 7/8  RD/Shell	Q2    net pft CCS   1274    1178/1367  1187</p>
<p> 7/8  RD/Shell	H1    net pft CCS   2784    2656/2912  2722</p>
<p>NOTES - Profit figures exclude extraordinary items and are in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated. They are stated before deduction of preference dividends where applicable.</p>
<p>Outlying estimates are sometimes excluded if they fall far outside the range of most forecasts.</p>
<p>* REED ELSEVIER figures refer to &quot;headline&quot; combined pre-tax profit and are in pounds sterling.</p>
<p>* ROYAL DUTCH/SHELL estimates are in millions of sterling and refer to historic cost net profit and current cost net profit excluding special items.</p>
<p>FORECASTS CONTRIBUTED BY: Amstgeld, Bangert Pontier, Delta Lloyd Bank, Generale Bank, ING, Kempen &amp; Co, Labouchere, Van Lanschot, Rabo/IRIS, SNS Securities, Wesselius.</p>
